    "absent": [
      "no consumer of the new column is exercised here: the deliverable is that per-lane queries are answerable without parsing payloads, and this node establishes the column, its index and the backfill; nothing routes a WHERE backend = ? through the store in this change, so an end-to-end per-lane query is untested. The index claim is asserted by EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN, which is the closest check reachable inside the node's declared scope.",
      "the added-failure derivation a coordinator reads automatically (reckon.crew.review.annotate_review_of_run) reads the reviewed manifest's armed baseline_suite/after_suite fields; this node ran unarmed and its template marks those fields armed-only, so that path reports the count as unmeasured (None) however this stored record reads. The delta in this record was derived by hand from the two arm logs the manifest names under test_logs, using the repository's own added_failures_from_gate_logs, and both raw logs survive on disk.",
      "the corpus totals are a snapshot taken at review time and move with the fleet: 6233 rows at the node's measurement, 6239 thirteen minutes later, both with the same 26 permanent NULLs. The 22 legacy non-NULL rows and the 26 NULLs are checked on a copy; no sqlite connection in this review opened the live store.",
      "the base and negative-control scratch trees under /tmp were read and re-run, not restored: /tmp is node-local, so those trees are evidence only for readers on this node."
